net: dsa: b53: mirror BPDUs to CPU port 5 when port 8 is not a CPU port

With port 5 as the CPU port, b53_brcm_hdr_setup() sets En_IMP_Port to 11:
dual-IMP mode. The BCM53125 data sheet (Global Management Configuration,
page 02h address 00h) says that in this mode the frames the switch traps for
the CPU, the BPDUs that En_RX_BPDU traps among them, go to the IMP port (8)
from LAN ports and to port 5 only from WAN ports.

The Control4 EA3 wires only port 5 to the SoC; port 8 is unconnected. So the
bridge on lan1/lan2 never received a BPDU, STP never saw a loop, and cabling
both jacks into one LAN took the box off the network.

Selecting the user ports as WAN ports does deliver the BPDUs, but a WAN
port's traffic goes to the CPU only: measured on an EA3, frames from lan1
stopped reaching lan2. So use the ingress mirror instead, filtered on the
STP group address, from the user ports to port 5. Measured on an EA3 with a
host sending BPDUs into lan1: stock, none reached the CPU and br-lan stayed
its own root; with the mirror, all of them did and br-lan took the sender as
root, while lan1 <-> lan2 forwarding kept working.

The switch has one mirror, so tc mirroring is refused while it holds.

diff -ruN a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c	2026-11-02 16:25:32
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c	2026-11-02 16:25:55
@@ -797,6 +797,24 @@
 		hdr_ctl |= GC_FRM_MGMT_PORT_M;
 	b53_write8(dev, B53_MGMT_PAGE, B53_GLOBAL_CONFIG, hdr_ctl);
 
+	/* Port 5 as CPU port puts BCM531x5 in dual-IMP mode, which traps the
+	 * BPDUs of LAN ports to the IMP port (8), not to port 5. When port 8
+	 * is not a CPU port nothing receives them, so STP never sees its peers
+	 * and never blocks a loop. Mirror them to port 5 instead. This takes
+	 * the switch's only mirror, so tc mirroring is refused while it holds.
+	 */
+	if (tag_en && port == 5 && is531x5(dev) &&
+	    !dsa_is_cpu_port(ds, B53_CPU_PORT)) {
+		b53_write48(dev, B53_MGMT_PAGE, B53_IG_MIR_MAC,
+			    ether_addr_to_u64(eth_stp_addr));
+		b53_write16(dev, B53_MGMT_PAGE, B53_IG_MIR_CTL,
+			    MIRROR_DA << MIRROR_FILTER_SHIFT |
+			    (dsa_user_ports(ds) & MIRROR_MASK));
+		b53_write16(dev, B53_MGMT_PAGE, B53_MIR_CAP_CTL,
+			    MIRROR_EN | port);
+		dev->bpdu_mirror = true;
+	}
+
 	/* B53_BRCM_HDR not present on devices with legacy tags */
 	if (dev->tag_protocol == DSA_TAG_PROTO_BRCM_LEGACY ||
 	    dev->tag_protocol == DSA_TAG_PROTO_BRCM_LEGACY_FCS)
@@ -2539,6 +2557,12 @@
 {
 	struct b53_device *dev = ds->priv;
 	u16 reg, loc;
+
+	if (dev->bpdu_mirror) {
+		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack,
+				   "Mirror carries BPDUs to CPU port 5");
+		return -EBUSY;
+	}
 
 	if (ingress)
 		loc = B53_IG_MIR_CTL;
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_priv.h b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_priv.h
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_priv.h	2026-11-02 16:25:32
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_priv.h	2026-11-02 16:25:35
@@ -169,6 +169,7 @@
 
 	/* run time configuration */
 	bool enable_jumbo;
+	bool bpdu_mirror;
 
 	unsigned int num_vlans;
 	struct b53_vlan *vlans;
